cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below. Once the paper is published, please also cite the article."
type: software
title: "Replication code and data for: Citizen Science on the Farm — Shared Observational Effort is Lacking on Agricultural Lands"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ngunner/citizen-science-on-the-farm"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   <- uncomment and fill in the CONCEPT DOI after the first Zenodo release
abstract: >-
  Code and data by Nicholas Gunner accompanying the article by Nicholas Gunner, Yu Jiang, Kaitlin Gold,
  Sara Emery and Terence Bates (Cornell AgriTech, Cornell University). Scripts, intermediate tables and derived county-level data that reproduce the analysis of citizen-science
  observational effort on agricultural land in the conterminous United States: the 2023 county-level
  observational disparity, 1 km coverage and Observational Effort Index (GBIF x USGS NLCD, county
  socioeconomics from USDA ERS), the 2014-2024 disparity time series (GBIF Maps API x USGS Annual NLCD in
  Google Earth Engine), and all script-generated figures.
authors:
  - family-names: Gunner
    given-names: Nicholas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5911-2124"
    affiliation: "Horticulture Section, School of Integrative Plant Science, Cornell AgriTech, Cornell University, Geneva, NY, USA"
keywords:
  - citizen science
  - GBIF
  - agriculture
  - biodiversity monitoring
  - spatial bias
  - National Land Cover Database
  - Google Earth Engine
  - observational effort
  - agroecology
  - United States
